xnu 0420: the frame queue's thread is woken by the GPU's fence interrupt instead of looking every 500 us

The thread of the frame queue (0340, kern.sweet_fb_queue=1) flips the oldest waiting frame once its GPU work is done
and the MDP has taken the flip before it; while a frame waits it looks every kern.sweet_fb_queue_poll_us (500 us),
~2000 wakeups a second at priority 81 during an animation. Report 16 §5.3 has an unnamed kernel thread of priority 81
waking every 0.63-0.71 ms (4-7 % of the idle entries of the A73 cluster); this thread fits [hypothesis].

With 0419's fence interrupt armed (kern.sweet_gpu_wait=2) the interrupt also wakes this thread: the thread registers
&fQThread, the event it sleeps on, with sapphire_gpu_fence_listener(), and gpu_spi() thread_wakeup()s it on every
CACHE_FLUSH_TS. While the oldest frame only waits for its GPU work (fQCount != 0, no flip waiting to be taken by the
MDP, frameDone() false) the thread then sleeps up to kern.sweet_fb_queue_irq_us (4000; clamped to 100-8000 like the
poll) instead of kern.sweet_fb_queue_poll_us. Waiting for the MDP to take a flip it still looks every poll period:
no display interrupt is used. Without the interrupt (sapphire_gpu_fence_irq() false, the default) nothing changes.

The thread is named "sweet fb queue" (thread_set_thread_name), so kdebug traces and thrsched tell it apart.
kern.sweet_fb_queue_irq_sleeps counts the sleeps the interrupt was to end.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index dec1b7f..7cf323d 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -323,6 +323,18 @@ static struct {
 	struct sweet_fbd_hist lat;              /* from the SwapEnd coming in to the flip, waits included */
 } sweet_fbq;
 extern uint32_t sapphire_gpu_copy_fence(void);          /* SapphireGpu.cpp: the fence of the last copy queued */
+/*
+ * sapphire 0420: with the GPU's fence interrupt (0419, kern.sweet_gpu_wait=2) every fence the GPU writes wakes the
+ * queue's thread (sapphire_gpu_fence_listener(&fQThread)), so while the oldest frame only waits for its GPU work
+ * (the MDP has taken the flip before it) the thread sleeps kern.sweet_fb_queue_irq_us (4000) instead of
+ * kern.sweet_fb_queue_poll_us (500): ~one wakeup per frame instead of one every 500 us. Waiting for the MDP to take a
+ * flip (no interrupt of the display is used) it still looks every kern.sweet_fb_queue_poll_us. Without the
+ * interrupt nothing changes. The thread is named "sweet fb queue" (thread_set_thread_name) for kdebug and thrsched.
+ */
+static int sweet_fb_queue_irq_us = 4000;
+static uint64_t sweet_fbq_irq_sleeps;
+extern "C" bool sapphire_gpu_fence_irq(void);           /* SapphireGpu.cpp (0419) */
+extern "C" void sapphire_gpu_fence_listener(void *event);
 extern bool sapphire_gpu_fence_done(uint32_t fence);    /* ... and whether a given one is done */
 
 /*
@@ -3298,6 +3310,8 @@ AppleCLCD::queueThreadMain(void *self, __unused wait_result_t result)
 void
 AppleCLCD::queueThread(void)
 {
+	thread_set_thread_name(current_thread(), "sweet fb queue");     /* 0420 */
+	sapphire_gpu_fence_listener(&fQThread);
 	IOLockLock(fPresentLock);
 	for (;;) {
 		if (fQCount != 0 || fQLatchWait) {
@@ -3308,6 +3322,10 @@ AppleCLCD::queueThread(void)
 		if (fQCount != 0 || (fQLatchWait && queueOn())) {
 			uint64_t deadline;
 			int us = sweet_fb_queue_poll_us;
+			if (fQCount != 0 && !fQLatchWait && sapphire_gpu_fence_irq() && !frameDone(&fQ[0], mach_absolute_time())) {
+				us = sweet_fb_queue_irq_us > us ? sweet_fb_queue_irq_us : us;   /* 0420: the fence's interrupt wakes it */
+				sweet_fbq_irq_sleeps++;
+			}
 			clock_interval_to_deadline((uint32_t)(us < 100 ? 100 : us > 8000 ? 8000 : us), kMicrosecondScale, &deadline);
 			(void)IOLockSleepDeadline(fPresentLock, &fQThread, deadline, THREAD_UNINT);
 			sweet_fbq.polls++;
@@ -4763,6 +4781,10 @@ SYSCTL_INT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_fb_queue_hold_ms, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED,
     "sapphire 0340: the longest a SwapEnd waits for a free flip buffer, ms (200 at most; 0 = never)");
 SYSCTL_INT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_fb_queue_poll_us, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fb_queue_poll_us, 0,
     "sapphire 0340: how often the queue's thread looks at a pending copy's fence, us (100 to 8000)");
+SYSCTL_INT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_fb_queue_irq_us, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fb_queue_irq_us, 0,
+    "sapphire 0420: with the GPU's fence interrupt, how long the queue's thread sleeps at most for a frame's GPU work, us (100 to 8000)");
+SYSCTL_QUAD(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_fb_queue_irq_sleeps, CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fbq_irq_sleeps,
+    "sapphire 0420: sleeps of the queue's thread that the fence interrupt was to end");
 SYSCTL_INT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_fb_queue_depth, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fb_queue_depth, 0,
     "sapphire 0340: how many frames may wait for the panel before a SwapEnd is held (1 or 2)");
 
